          },
          "worked": "Long division successively gives quotient terms $3x^3$, $-6x^2$, $10x$ and $-19$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x^4-2x^2+x-3-(x+2)(3x^3)&=-6x^3-2x^2+x-3\\\\-6x^3-2x^2+x-3-(x+2)(-6x^2)&=10x^2+x-3\\\\10x^2+x-3-(x+2)(10x)&=-19x-3\\\\-19x-3-(x+2)(-19)&=35\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q(x)=3x^3-6x^2+10x-19$ and $R(x)=35$.\n$$P(x)=(x+2)(3x^3-6x^2+10x-19)+35.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
