          },
          "worked": "Long division successively gives quotient terms $2x^2$, $4x$ and $-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^4+4x^3-2x^2+x+1-(x^2+2)(2x^2)&=4x^3-6x^2+x+1\\\\4x^3-6x^2+x+1-(x^2+2)(4x)&=-6x^2-7x+1\\\\-6x^2-7x+1-(x^2+2)(-6)&=-7x+13\\end{align*}$$\nThe remainder has degree $1<2$. Thus $Q(x)=2x^2+4x-6$ and $R(x)=-7x+13$.\n$$P(x)=(x^2+2)(2x^2+4x-6)-7x+13.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-task-17-21-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^2+3x+5,\\quad D(x)=x-1$",
