          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^3+3x^2-2x+4-(x+3)(2x^2)&=-3x^2-2x+4\\\\-3x^2-2x+4-(x+3)(-3x)&=7x+4\\\\7x+4-(x+3)7&=-17\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q(x)=2x^2-3x+7$ and $R(x)=-17$.\n$$P(x)=(x+3)(2x^2-3x+7)-17.$$",
