          "worked": "Use $P(x)=x^3+0x^2+0x+1$ for long division.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3+1-(x+2)x^2&=-2x^2+1\\\\-2x^2+1-(x+2)(-2x)&=4x+1\\\\4x+1-(x+2)4&=-7\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q(x)=x^2-2x+4$ and $R(x)=-7$.\n$$P(x)=(x+2)(x^2-2x+4)-7.$$",
